window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-11ef3e151227c2a8"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"troubleshooting\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">故障排查</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 后追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该文档的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"frequently-asked-questions\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">常见问题</h2> <p><a id=\"files-appear-in-the-side-panel-that-codex-didnt-edit\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex\">侧边栏中出现 Codex 没有编辑过的文件</h3> <p>如果项目位于 Git 仓库中，审查面板会根据项目的 Git 状态自动显示更改，其中也可能包括并非由 Codex 所做的更改。</p> <p>在审查面板中，你可以切换已暂存的更改和未暂存的更改，也可以将当前分支与 main 比较。</p> <p>如果只想查看 Codex 最近一轮造成的更改，请将差异面板切换到 <strong>Last turn</strong> 视图。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-47b0440a51c2fc92\">了解如何使用审查面板</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"remove-a-project-from-the-sidebar\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_3\">从侧边栏移除项目</h3> <p>要从侧边栏移除项目，请将鼠标悬停在项目名称上，选择三点菜单，然后选择 <strong>Remove</strong>。要恢复项目，请使用 <strong>Chats</strong> 旁边的 <strong>Add new project</strong> 按钮重新添加，或使用</p> <p><kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>O</kbd>。</p> <p><a id=\"find-archived-threads\"></a> <a id=\"find-archived-tasks\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"find-archived-chats\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">查找已归档的对话</h3> <p>已归档的对话可以在设置（已阻止不安全链接）中找到。取消归档后，对话会回到侧边栏原来的位置。</p> <p><a id=\"a-work-conversation-does-not-appear-on-another-device\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"work\">Work 对话未显示在另一台设备上</h3> <ul> <li>确认每台设备都使用同一个 ChatGPT 账户和工作区登录。</li> <li>请工作区所有者确认已启用 Work Cloud 和 <strong>Allow local computer access</strong>。如果任一云端策略启用了 <code>enforce_residency</code>，Work 和 dots 的 <strong>Allow local computer access</strong> 都会被禁用。这项保护措施不会配置工作区驻留，也不会单独关闭 Work Cloud 或 dots。</li> <li>查看任务创建时间。同步仅适用于启用后新建的任务。已有任务（包括项目中的任务）不会迁移，仍保留原有的仅本地模式，或无法访问本地文件的云端模式。</li> </ul> <p>对于企业版用户，应用内的 Local/Cloud 切换开关及其默认设置在功能上线时保持不变。某个切换开关或默认模式本身不能证明对话是否可以同步。查找 Work 对话时，请勿与 Codex 历史记录混淆。设置请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d50d47c21e8fd4ad\">Work Cloud 和 dots 的本地计算机访问</a>；常见问题请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-b498643ba7f3888a\">Work 管理员常见问题</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"a-synced-task-cannot-use-the-computers-files-or-tools\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">同步任务无法使用电脑上的文件或工具</h3> <p>让电脑保持联网并连接。如果新一轮任务开始时电脑不可用，符合条件的同步任务可以在云容器中继续运行，但无法访问电脑上的文件或工具。正在运行的一轮不会自动从电脑切换到云端。</p> <p><a id=\"a-turn-stopped-after-local-computer-access-was-turned-off\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"a-turn-stopped-after-local-computer-access-with-work-cloud-was-turned-off\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"work-cloud\">关闭 Work Cloud 本地计算机访问后，一轮任务停止了</h3> <p>关闭 Work Cloud 本地计算机访问会中断正在运行的轮次。如果你仍有 Work 访问权，请发送新消息以开始新一轮。在已有云端对话中，新一轮会自动使用无法访问本地文件的 Work Cloud。</p> <p><a id=\"automated-policy-updates-are-missing\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">自动化策略更新没有生效</h3> <p>使用策略 API 管理 Global 设置；使用 Agent Security 界面管理 Local 或 Codex Cloud 设置。迁移后，现有 Global API 工作流仍可使用。请测试脚本和 Terraform 集成，并确认策略分配和排序没有改变。</p> <p><a id=\"only-some-threads-appear-in-the-sidebar\"></a> <a id=\"only-some-tasks-appear-in-the-sidebar\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"only-some-chats-appear-in-the-sidebar\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_7\">侧边栏只显示部分对话</h3> <p>侧边栏可以根据项目状态筛选对话。如果有对话不见了，请选择 <strong>Chats</strong> 旁的筛选图标，然后选择 <strong>Chronological</strong>。如果仍找不到，请打开设置（已阻止不安全链接），检查 <strong>Archived chats</strong>。</p> <p><a id=\"code-doesnt-run-on-a-worktree\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"worktree\">在 worktree 中无法运行代码</h3> <p>worktree 位于不同目录中，默认会继承 Git 中登记的文件。根据项目管理依赖项和工具的方式，你可能需要使用<a href=\"#/article/a-86cde8be2e24d05a\">本地环境</a>在 worktree 中运行设置脚本，或使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-d955137d94c4d306?anchor=copy-ignored-local-files-into-managed-worktrees\"><code>.worktreeinclude</code></a>复制被忽略的设置文件。你也可以在常规本地项目中检出这些更改。详情请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-d955137d94c4d306\">worktree 文档</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"app-doesnt-pick-up-a-teammates-shared-local-environment\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_8\">应用没有采用队友共享的本地环境</h3> <p>本地环境配置必须位于项目根目录下的 <code>.codex</code> 文件夹中。如果你在包含多个项目的 monorepo 中工作，请确保打开的是包含 <code>.codex</code> 文件夹的项目目录。</p> <p><a id=\"codex-asks-to-access-apple-music\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex-apple-music\">Codex 请求访问 Apple Music</h3> <p>根据任务需要，Codex 可能需要浏览文件系统。在 macOS 上，Music、Downloads 或 Desktop 等某些目录需要用户额外批准访问。如果 Codex 需要读取你的主目录，macOS 会提示你批准访问这些文件夹。</p> <p><a id=\"automations-create-many-worktrees\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"scheduled-tasks-create-many-worktrees\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"worktree_1\">计划任务创建了很多 worktree</h3> <p>频繁运行计划任务可能会逐渐创建许多 worktree。请归档不再需要的计划运行记录；除非打算保留其 worktree，否则不要将运行记录固定在侧边栏。</p> <p><a id=\"recover-a-prompt-after-selecting-the-wrong-target\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">选错目标后恢复提示内容</h3> <p>如果你不小心为对话选错了目标（<strong>Local</strong>、<strong>Worktree</strong> 或 <strong>Cloud</strong>），可以取消当前运行，然后在输入框中按向上箭头恢复之前的提示内容。</p> <p><a id=\"approve-for-me-is-missing-or-disabled\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"approve-for-me\">Approve for me（代为批准）不见了或被禁用</h3> <p>要使用自动审查，请在输入框下方的权限控件中选择 <strong>Approve for me（代为批准）</strong>。如果该模式不见了或被禁用：</p> <ol> <li>更新桌面应用，并在希望使用自动审查的那个对话中检查权限菜单。本地与云端环境提供的选项可能不同。</li> <li>对于本地 Codex 执行，检查实际生效的配置中是否明确设置了 <code>features.guardian_approval = false</code>，并核对已配置的权限配置文件、审批策略和审批审查者。配置优先级请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">配置基础</a>。本地配置不能控制托管的云端运行时。</li> <li>如果托管工作区中的模式被禁用或缺失，请管理员检查允许的权限配置文件、沙箱模式、审批策略和审批审查者。组织或设备策略可以限制这些选项；本地设置不能覆盖这些限制。</li> </ol> <p>如果该模式仍然异常不可用，请在<a href=\"#/article/a-11ef3e151227c2a8?anchor=feedback-and-logs\">反馈</a>中说明应用版本、操作系统、执行环境，以及该选项是缺失还是被禁用。</p> <p><a id=\"feature-is-working-in-the-codex-cli-but-not-in-the-chatgpt-desktop-app\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex-cli-chatgpt\">功能在 Codex CLI 中可用，但在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中不可用</h3> <p>ChatGPT 桌面应用和 Codex CLI 中包含的 Codex 版本可能不同，因此功能可能先后到达不同界面。</p> <p>要查看系统中的 Codex CLI 版本，请运行：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex --version\n</code></pre> <p>要查看 ChatGPT 桌面应用内置的 Codex 版本，请使用保留的 <code>Codex.app</code> 兼容包路径：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">/Applications/Codex.app/Contents/Resources/codex --version\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"feedback-and-logs\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">反馈与日志</h2> <p>在消息输入框中输入 <kbd>/</kbd>，即可向团队提交反馈。如果你在已有对话中提交反馈，可以选择同时分享现有会话。提交后，你会收到一个会话 ID，可以提供给团队。</p> <p>报告问题：</p> <ol> <li>在 Codex GitHub 代码库中查找<a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">现有问题（需联网）</a>。</li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/new?template=2-bug-report.yml&amp;steps=Uploaded%20thread%3A%20019c0d37-d2b6-74c0-918f-0e64af9b6e14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">新建 GitHub 问题（需联网）</a>。</li> </ol> <p>更多日志位于以下位置：</p> <ul> <li>应用日志（macOS）：<code>~/Library/Logs/com.openai.codex/YYYY/MM/DD</code></li> <li>会话记录：<code>$CODEX_HOME/sessions</code>（默认：<code>~/.codex/sessions</code>）</li> <li>已归档会话：<code>$CODEX_HOME/archived_sessions</code>（默认：<code>~/.codex/archived_sessions</code>）</li> </ul> <p>分享日志前，请先检查其中是否含有敏感信息。</p> <p><a id=\"stuck-states-and-recovery-patterns\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">卡住的状态与恢复方法</h2> <p>如果对话似乎卡住了：</p> <ol> <li>检查 Codex 是否正在等待审批。</li> <li>打开终端并运行 <code>git status</code> 等基本命令。</li> <li>使用更小、更聚焦的提示开始新对话。</li> </ol> <p>如果不小心取消了 worktree 创建并丢失提示内容，请在输入框中按向上箭头恢复。</p> <p><a id=\"terminal-issues\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_12\">终端问题</h2> <p><strong>终端似乎卡住了</strong></p> <ol> <li>关闭终端面板。</li> <li>按 <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>`</kbd> 重新打开终端。</li> <li>重新运行 <code>pwd</code> 或 <code>git status</code> 等基本命令。</li> </ol> <p>如果命令运行结果与预期不同，请先检查终端中的当前目录和分支。</p> <p>如果问题仍然存在，请等当前活动对话完成后再重启应用。</p> <p><strong>字体显示不正确</strong></p> <p>Codex 的审查面板、集成终端以及应用中显示的其他代码使用相同字体。你可以在设置（已阻止不安全链接）窗格中通过 <strong>Code font</strong> 配置该字体。</p> <p><a id=\"an-environment-allows-network-access-but-the-action-is-blocked\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_13\">环境允许网络访问，但操作仍被阻止</h2> <p>比较单项设置前，请先检查策略优先级。即使低优先级策略更具体，高优先级策略仍优先生效。在单个策略内部，操作系统专属环境覆盖项优先于全操作系统环境覆盖项，后者又优先于 Global。</p> <p>某些网络要求有字段专属的合并规则和运行时限制。云端运行时不支持托管 HTTP/SOCKS 监听端口和非回环代理监听端口；套接字规则是否受支持取决于执行路径。本地执行的合并行为另行处理。</p> <p>请比较实际生效的策略，并测试预期允许或阻止的操作。详细情况请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">托管配置</a>。不要为了绕过测试失败而扩大 Global 基准范围。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"troubleshooting\">Troubleshooting</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently Asked Questions</h2> <h3 id=\"files-appear-in-the-side-panel-that-codex-didnt-edit\">Files appear in the side panel that Codex didn't edit</h3> <p>If your project is inside a Git repository, the review panel automatically shows changes based on your project's Git state, including changes that Codex didn't make.</p> <p>In the review pane, you can switch between staged changes and changes not yet staged, and compare your branch with main.</p> <p>If you want to see only the changes of your last Codex turn, switch the diff pane to the <strong>Last turn</strong> view.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-47b0440a51c2fc92\">Learn more about how to use the review pane</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"remove-a-project-from-the-sidebar\">Remove a project from the sidebar</h3> <p>To remove a project from the sidebar, hover over the name of your project, select the three dots, and choose <strong>Remove</strong>. To restore it, re-add the project using the <strong>Add new project</strong> button next to <strong>Chats</strong> or using</p> <p><kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>O</kbd>.</p> <p><a id=\"find-archived-threads\"></a> <a id=\"find-archived-tasks\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"find-archived-chats\">Find archived chats</h3> <p>Archived chats can be found in Settings (blocked unsafe link). When you unarchive a chat, it reappears in its original sidebar location.</p> <h3 id=\"a-work-conversation-does-not-appear-on-another-device\">A Work conversation does not appear on another device</h3> <ul> <li>Confirm that you are signed in with ChatGPT to the same account and workspace on each device.</li> <li>Ask your workspace owner to check that Work Cloud and <strong>Allow local computer access</strong> are enabled. If <code>enforce_residency</code> is enabled in any cloud policy, <strong>Allow local computer access</strong> is disabled for both Work and dots. This safeguard does not configure workspace residency or, by itself, disable Work Cloud or dots.</li> <li>Check when the task was created. Sync applies to new tasks created after it is enabled. Existing tasks, including tasks in projects, are not migrated and keep their original local-only or cloud-without-local-files behavior.</li> </ul> <p>For enterprises, the in-app Local/Cloud toggle and its default remain unchanged at launch. A particular toggle or default mode does not by itself confirm whether a conversation can sync. Keep Codex history separate when looking for a Work conversation. See <a href=\"#/article/a-d50d47c21e8fd4ad\">Local computer access for Work Cloud and dots</a> for setup and the <a href=\"#/article/a-b498643ba7f3888a\">Work admin FAQ</a> for common questions.</p> <h3 id=\"a-synced-task-cannot-use-the-computers-files-or-tools\">A synced task cannot use the computer's files or tools</h3> <p>Keep the computer online and connected. If it's unavailable when a new turn starts, an eligible synced task can continue in a cloud container without access to the computer's files or tools. A running turn doesn't automatically move from the computer to the cloud.</p> <p><a id=\"a-turn-stopped-after-local-computer-access-was-turned-off\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"a-turn-stopped-after-local-computer-access-with-work-cloud-was-turned-off\">A turn stopped after Local computer access with Work Cloud was turned off</h3> <p>Turning off Local computer access with Work Cloud interrupts running turns. If you still have Work access, send a new message to start another turn. In an existing cloud conversation, that turn automatically uses Work Cloud without access to local files.</p> <h3 id=\"automated-policy-updates-are-missing\">Automated policy updates are missing</h3> <p>Use the policy API to manage Global settings. To manage Local or Codex Cloud settings, use the Agent Security UI. Existing Global API workflows remain available after migration. Test your scripts and Terraform integrations, and confirm that policy assignments and ordering are unchanged.</p> <p><a id=\"only-some-threads-appear-in-the-sidebar\"></a> <a id=\"only-some-tasks-appear-in-the-sidebar\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"only-some-chats-appear-in-the-sidebar\">Only some chats appear in the sidebar</h3> <p>The sidebar lets you filter chats based on the state of a project. If you're missing chats, select the filter icon next to <strong>Chats</strong>, then select <strong>Chronological</strong>. If you still don't see the chat, open Settings (blocked unsafe link) and check <strong>Archived chats</strong>.</p> <h3 id=\"code-doesnt-run-on-a-worktree\">Code doesn't run on a worktree</h3> <p>Worktrees are created in a different directory and inherit files checked into Git by default. Depending on how you manage dependencies and tooling for your project, you might have to run setup scripts on your worktree using a <a href=\"#/article/a-86cde8be2e24d05a\">local environment</a> or copy ignored setup files with <a href=\"#/article/a-d955137d94c4d306?anchor=copy-ignored-local-files-into-managed-worktrees\"><code>.worktreeinclude</code></a>. You can also check out the changes in your regular local project. See the <a href=\"#/article/a-d955137d94c4d306\">worktrees documentation</a> to learn more.</p> <h3 id=\"app-doesnt-pick-up-a-teammates-shared-local-environment\">App doesn't pick up a teammate's shared local environment</h3> <p>The local environment configuration must be inside the <code>.codex</code> folder at the root of your project. If you are working in a monorepo with more than one project, make sure you open the project in the directory that contains the <code>.codex</code> folder.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-asks-to-access-apple-music\">Codex asks to access Apple Music</h3> <p>Depending on your task, Codex may need to navigate the file system. Certain directories on macOS, including Music, Downloads, or Desktop, require additional approval from the user. If Codex needs to read your home directory, macOS prompts you to approve access to those folders.</p> <p><a id=\"automations-create-many-worktrees\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"scheduled-tasks-create-many-worktrees\">Scheduled tasks create many worktrees</h3> <p>Frequent scheduled tasks can create many worktrees over time. Archive scheduled runs you no longer need and avoid pinning runs unless you intend to keep their worktrees.</p> <h3 id=\"recover-a-prompt-after-selecting-the-wrong-target\">Recover a prompt after selecting the wrong target</h3> <p>If you started a chat with the wrong target (<strong>Local</strong>, <strong>Worktree</strong>, or <strong>Cloud</strong>) by accident, you can cancel the current run and recover your previous prompt by pressing the up arrow key in the composer.</p> <h3 id=\"approve-for-me-is-missing-or-disabled\">Approve for me is missing or disabled</h3> <p>To use automatic review, select <strong>Approve for me</strong> from the permissions control below the composer. If the mode is missing or disabled:</p> <ol> <li>Update the desktop app and check the permissions menu in the chat where you want to use automatic review. The available choices can differ between local and cloud environments.</li> <li>For local Codex execution, check your effective configuration for an explicit <code>features.guardian_approval = false</code> setting and review the configured permission profile, approval policy, and approval reviewer. See <a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">Config basics</a> for configuration precedence. Local configuration doesn't control a managed cloud runtime.</li> <li>If a mode is disabled or missing in a managed workspace, ask your administrator to check the allowed permission profiles, sandbox modes, approval policies, and approval reviewers. Organization or device policy can restrict these choices; local settings can't override it.</li> </ol> <p>If the mode is still unexpectedly unavailable, include your app version, operating system, execution environment, and whether the option is missing or disabled in your <a href=\"#/article/a-11ef3e151227c2a8?anchor=feedback-and-logs\">feedback</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"feature-is-working-in-the-codex-cli-but-not-in-the-chatgpt-desktop-app\">Feature is working in the Codex CLI but not in the ChatGPT desktop app</h3> <p>The ChatGPT desktop app and Codex CLI can include different Codex versions, so features may reach one surface before the other.</p> <p>To get the version of the Codex CLI on your system run:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex --version\n</code></pre> <p>To get the version of Codex bundled with your ChatGPT desktop app, use the retained <code>Codex.app</code> compatibility bundle path:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">/Applications/Codex.app/Contents/Resources/codex --version\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"feedback-and-logs\">Feedback and logs</h2> <p>Type <kbd>/</kbd> into the message composer to provide feedback for the team. If you trigger feedback in an existing chat, you can choose to share the existing session along with your feedback. After submitting your feedback, you'll receive a session ID that you can share with the team.</p> <p>To report an issue:</p> <ol> <li>Find <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">existing issues (online)</a> on the Codex GitHub repo.</li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/new?template=2-bug-report.yml&amp;steps=Uploaded%20thread%3A%20019c0d37-d2b6-74c0-918f-0e64af9b6e14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open a new GitHub issue (online)</a></li> </ol> <p>More logs are available in the following locations:</p> <ul> <li>App logs (macOS): <code>~/Library/Logs/com.openai.codex/YYYY/MM/DD</code></li> <li>Session transcripts: <code>$CODEX_HOME/sessions</code> (default: <code>~/.codex/sessions</code>)</li> <li>Archived sessions: <code>$CODEX_HOME/archived_sessions</code> (default: <code>~/.codex/archived_sessions</code>)</li> </ul> <p>If you share logs, review them first to confirm they don't contain sensitive information.</p> <h2 id=\"stuck-states-and-recovery-patterns\">Stuck states and recovery patterns</h2> <p>If a chat appears stuck:</p> <ol> <li>Check whether Codex is waiting for an approval.</li> <li>Open the terminal and run a basic command like <code>git status</code>.</li> <li>Start a new chat with a smaller, more focused prompt.</li> </ol> <p>If you cancel worktree creation by mistake and lose your prompt, press the up arrow key in the composer to recover it.</p> <h2 id=\"terminal-issues\">Terminal issues</h2> <p><strong>Terminal appears stuck</strong></p> <ol> <li>Close the terminal panel.</li> <li>Reopen it with <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>`</kbd>.</li> <li>Re-run a basic command like <code>pwd</code> or <code>git status</code>.</li> </ol> <p>If commands behave differently than expected, check the current directory and branch in the terminal first.</p> <p>If it continues to be stuck, wait until your active chats are complete and restart the app.</p> <p><strong>Fonts aren't rendering correctly</strong></p> <p>Codex uses the same font for the review pane, integrated terminal and any other code displayed inside the app. You can configure the font inside the Settings (blocked unsafe link) pane as <strong>Code font</strong>.</p> <h2 id=\"an-environment-allows-network-access-but-the-action-is-blocked\">An environment allows network access but the action is blocked</h2> <p>Check policy priority before comparing individual settings. A higher-priority policy wins over a lower-priority policy, even if the lower-priority policy is more specific. Within one policy, OS-specific environment overrides take priority over all-OS environment overrides, followed by Global.</p> <p>Some network requirements have field-specific merge rules and runtime limits. Managed HTTP/SOCKS listener ports and non-loopback proxy listeners are unsupported by the cloud runtime; socket-rule support depends on the execution path. Local-execution merge behavior is separate.</p> <p>Compare the effective policies and test the intended allowed and blocked actions. See <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">Managed configuration</a> for the detailed cases. Do not broaden the global baseline to work around a failed test.</p>"};
